  "term": "striate cortex",
  "definition": "The striate cortex is the primary visual area of the human visual cortex, located in parts of the occipital lobe and along the calcarine sulcus. It receives direct input from the lateral geniculate nucleus and is the cortical area where visual signals first arrive.",
